# npm hands scripts to cmd.exe on Windows, and cmd.exe treats "&" as a command
# separator. This repo lives under a path containing "&" (TF&TE), so npm's
# PATH interpolation gets split mid-path and every `npm run` fails with
# "'TE\frontend\node_modules\.bin\' is not recognized".
#
# Git Bash does not split on "&", so scripts run intact.
#
# NOTE: this path is specific to this machine — Git is installed under
# C:\Users\initi\Git rather than C:\Program Files\Git. CI runs on Linux and
# ignores this file. The durable fix is renaming the directory to remove the
# "&"; see the README.
script-shell=C:\Users\initi\Git\bin\bash.exe
